## 4. FFmpeg — external tool, NOT distributed (license-relevant)

Video import/export shells out to an `ffmpeg` binary found on `PATH`.
Kagari VFX **does not link, embed, or ship FFmpeg**:

- No `ffmpeg-sys` / statically linked libav* anywhere in `Cargo.lock`.
- `bundle_dmg.sh` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` bundle only the
  Kagari binaries (verified 2026-09-13).
- Our invocations request encoders such as `libx264`, `libx265`,
  `prores_ks`, and `aac`. Whether those exist — and under which license
  the local FFmpeg was built (e.g. Homebrew `--enable-gpl`) — is purely
  a property of **the user's own FFmpeg install**, not of this project.
- If you redistribute Kagari VFX **together with** an FFmpeg binary
  (e.g. an all-in-one installer), that bundle triggers FFmpeg's own
  GPL/LGPL obligations. Either ship `ffmpeg`'s sources + build scripts
  alongside, or switch our invocations to non-GPL encoders
  (`mpeg4`, `libvpx-vp9`, `aac` via the native encoder) before bundling.

## 5. Coverage gaps in this audit

41 platform-specific crates (Linux `alsa`/`zbus`/`wayland-backend`,
Windows `windows-*`, Android `ndk`/`oboe`, plus `cc`, `futures-*`,
`nix`, `quick-xml`) were not present in the local registry cache and
could not be machine-verified here. They are all published under MIT /
Apache-2.0 upstream, but re-run the scan (`Cargo.lock` → registry
metadata) before cutting release binaries for those targets.

